Provide three functional choices:

1. SOMENTE LETRA BASTÃO

Brazilian Portuguese label:

“Somente letra bastão, em caixa alta”

Requirements:

• convert all student-facing text to uppercase;
• use a clear sans-serif font;
• use direct sentences;
• use increased spacing;
• avoid decorative distractions;
• preserve official skill codes as originally stored;
• preserve URLs, technical identifiers, and references when case changes would damage them.

2. LETRA BASTÃO + DESENHO RELACIONADO À MATRIZ

Brazilian Portuguese label:

“Letra bastão com desenho relacionado ao conteúdo”

Requirements:

• all student-facing instructions in uppercase;
• educational illustration linked to the curriculum content;
• illustration linked to the knowledge object;
• illustration linked to the selected skill;
• visual must serve a pedagogical purpose;
• no irrelevant decorative images;
• allow color illustration;
• allow black-and-white line art for coloring or interpretation;
• preserve adequate answer space;
• provide digital alternative text;
• maintain print quality;
• preserve readability in grayscale.

3. LETRA CURSIVA PEDAGÓGICA

Brazilian Portuguese label:

“Letra cursiva pedagógica”

Requirements:

• use a readable school handwriting style;
• include handwriting guide lines when requested;
• allow dotted or dashed tracing text;
• preserve curriculum content;
• provide a reliable PDF-safe font fallback;
• do not depend exclusively on an online font that may disappear during PDF export;
• test accented Brazilian Portuguese characters;
• allow the Teacher to preview and replace the selected cursive font.

Do not label a generic script font as pedagogically suitable without checking readability, accents, PDF embedding, and print output.

STEP 3 — VISUAL OPTION

If the Teacher selects drawing support, ask:

• color illustration;
• black-and-white illustration;
• drawing for interpretation;
• drawing for completion;
• drawing as answer;
• drawing for coloring with a pedagogical purpose;
• free drawing space;
• guided drawing.

STEP 4 — SUPPORT LEVEL

